<title>SWEDEN: Key forecasts in Sweden's 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Key forecasts in Sweden's 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the key economic forecasts in the Swedish government's budget for 1997. Comparison from the last budget in April 1996 are in brackets.</p>
<p>				    1996	   1997	 1998</p>
<p> GDP growth		   1.6  (1.4)   2.3  (2.0)    2.6  (2.5)</p>
<p> GDP (bln SKR)		1,692	  1,774	   1,867</p>
<p> Private consumption	0.9  (0.8)   1.8  (1.7)    2.4  (2.2)</p>
<p> Public consumption	-1.0  (0.9)  -0.5 (-1.1)   -1.2 (-1.2)</p>
<p> Gross fixed investment   8.1 (10.0)   2.0  (2.4)    8.5  (7.4)</p>
<p> Stockbuilding	     -1.5 (-1.0)   0.5  (0.1)    0.1  (0.0)</p>
<p> Exports			6.5  (4.5)   5.6   (6.1)   5.6  (5.4)</p>
<p> Imports			2.7  (5.0)   4.9   (4.7)   6.3  (5.3)</p>
<p> Trade balance (bln SKR)124.4	  139.6</p>
<p> CPI, Dec-Dec		 1.0 (1.9)    2.2   (2.3)   2.2  (2.2)</p>
<p> Unemployment		 7.7  (7.2)   6.9   (6.5)   6.1  (6.1)</p>
<p> Househd net saving ratio 8.5  (8.3)   7.5   (7.0)   6.5  (6.2)</p>
<p>GOVERNMENT FINANCE - percentage GDP</p>
<p> Revenue		     63.3	   62.1	    61.8</p>
<p> Expenditure		 67.2	   64.7	    61.9</p>
<p> Financial balance	 -4.0	   -2.6	     0.0</p>
<p> Primary Balance	   -1.8	   -1.1	     1.5</p>
<p> Borrowing need	     2.4	    3.1	     0.3</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
